The spec says: "No duplicates. At most 50 bookmarks per user." The developer wrote five acceptance tests before prompting the agent, and all of them pass on the agent's code:

  ✓ add then list returns the lesson
  ✓ list is most recent first
  ✓ adding the same lesson twice returns "already_bookmarked"
  ✓ the 51st bookmark returns "limit_reached"
  ✓ an unknown lesson returns "lesson_not_found"

The agent's add():

add(userId: string, lessonId: string, at: number): AddResult {
  if (!this.lessons.has(lessonId)) return "lesson_not_found";
  const bookmarks = this.byUser.get(userId) ?? [];
  if (bookmarks.length >= 50) return "limit_reached";
  if (bookmarks.some((b) => b.lessonId === lessonId)) return "already_bookmarked";
  bookmarks.push({ lessonId, at });
  this.byUser.set(userId, bookmarks);
  return "added";
}

Statement: "Because all five acceptance tests pass, a user who has 50 bookmarks and taps Bookmark on a lesson that is already in the list gets \"already_bookmarked\"."

Before prompting the agent, the developer wrote this test and a stub service whose add() returns "added", remove() returns "removed" and list() returns []:

// tests/bookmarks.test.ts
it("remove is idempotent", () => {
  const s = new BookmarkService(["les_101"]);
  s.add("u_ana", "les_101", 1000);
  expect(s.remove("u_ana", "les_101")).toBe("removed");
  expect(s.remove("u_ana", "les_101")).toBe("not_bookmarked");
});

$ npx vitest run tests/bookmarks.test.ts
 FAIL  tests/bookmarks.test.ts > remove is idempotent
AssertionError: expected 'removed' to be 'not_bookmarked'

After the agent's change the same command prints a pass, and git diff shows that tests/bookmarks.test.ts was not modified.

Statement: "This red run shows that the second assertion is able to fail, so the later green run is evidence that the agent's code, not the test, changed the result."
